PHH poker hand history corpus
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Copyright the University of Toronto Computer Poker Research Group.
Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0).
https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10796885

The corpus includes the 10,000 hands released with Brown & Sandholm, "Superhuman
AI for multiplayer poker" (Science, 2019) — one Pluribus seat against five human
professionals, six-handed, 100 big blinds, no ante.

**How it is used.** Aggregate frequencies measured from those hands — how often
each seat opens, how often each seat defends — are fitting targets for the
parameters of `ranges.tag.gen.py`. No range, grid or per-hand decision from the
corpus is copied into `ranges.tag.json`; which hands make up every range in that
file comes from this project's own equity table and model. CC-BY-4.0 permits
derivative works, and this notice is the attribution it requires.

The corpus itself is not redistributed here: `data/` is gitignored.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Not included in this repository
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This project deliberately excludes third-party material that is not ours to
redistribute. In particular, no solver source is vendored or linked: solvers
such as TexasSolver (AGPL-3.0) are run strictly out-of-process, and no
AGPL/GPL code is a build or runtime dependency of any crate in this workspace.
Chart data shipped here (`ranges.tag.json`) is generated by
`ranges.tag.gen.py` in this repository. See REPO_SEPARATION.md.

